<article class="env-lemma" id="046V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/046V">Lemma <span data-tag="046V">10.35.12</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $S$ be a $k$-algebra. For any field extension $K/k$ whose cardinality is larger than the cardinality of $S$ we have </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $S_ K$ the field $\kappa (\mathfrak m)$ is algebraic over $K$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S_ K$ is a Jacobson ring. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $k \subset K$ such that the cardinality of $K$ is greater than the cardinality of $S$. Since the elements of $S$ generate the $K$-algebra $S_ K$ we see that Theorem <a href="/tag/00FU" data-tag="00FU">10.35.11</a> applies. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>